Package: homelab-backup-server
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10), python3-yaml, borgbackup, adduser, openssh-server, homelab-cli
Replaces: homelab-borg-service-backup-server
Breaks: homelab-borg-service-backup-server (<< 0.4.0)
Conflicts: borgbackup2
Description: Homelab service/config backup server built on borg
 Centralized-server counterpart to homelab-backup-client. Installing
 this package creates the borgbackup system user/group and backup
 directory. Client hosts enroll themselves via the homelab-api control
 plane (`homelab-cli backup enroll`); this server's own
 `homelab-backup-server-reconcile.timer` polls for pending enroll/revoke
 requests and applies them by granting/removing SSH access, restricted
 via a forced `borg serve --restrict-to-repository` command -- client
 hosts never need direct SSH or sudo access to this server. Run
 `homelab-backup-server setup` after installing to connect to the
 control plane and enable that timer.
 `enroll`/`list`/`revoke`/`admin-recovery-key` remain available for
 manual/emergency use without the control plane.
